{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter9#thm:gauss-bonnet-formula","title":"thm:gauss-bonnet-formula","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter9.md","line":20,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter9.tex#thm:gauss-bonnet-formula","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:arc-length-integral]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter9#thm:rotation-index-theorem]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter9#lem:rotation-index-plus-one]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prob:arc-length-integral]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter9.tex","label":"thm:gauss-bonnet-formula","line":254,"source":"\\begin{theorem}[The Gauss--Bonnet Formula]\n\\label{thm:gauss-bonnet-formula}\n\\uses{prop:arc-length-integral, thm:rotation-index-theorem, lem:rotation-index-plus-one, prob:arc-length-integral}\n\\dcref{ch9:9.3}\n\nLet $\\gamma$ be a positively oriented curved polygon in an oriented\nRiemannian $2$-manifold, with interior $\\Omega$ and exterior angles\n$\\varepsilon_1,\\ldots,\\varepsilon_k$.  Then\n\\begin{equation}\n\\int_\\Omega K\\,dA+\\int_\\gamma\\kappa_N\\,ds\n+\\sum_{i=1}^k\\varepsilon_i=2\\pi, \\tag{9.6}\n\\end{equation}\nwhere $K$ is Gaussian curvature, $dA$ is the oriented Riemannian area form,\nand the boundary integral is with respect to arc length.\n\\end{theorem}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Theorem</div></section>[The Gauss--Bonnet Formula] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-74686d3a67617573732d626f6e6e65742d666f726d756c61\"></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aarc-length-integral\">↗ prop:arc-lengt